export const MARASEN_RECORDS={
 mill:[
 ['The mill without a levy','A stone beneath the race carries Ismail’s order: leave one bank uncut, let the brook keep its bends, and never take the nursery seed for a marching column. That is why this side of the hills is green. The mill has stopped because a survey crew pulled out its regulating stones to weigh ammunition wagons. Three households now carry grain across the ridge by hand. Hugh has kept their flour separate from the Common Cause stores. Restoring the wheel will help families on both sides.','A scratched diagram names the three channels ROOT, WHEEL and OVERFLOW. The root feeder must receive the smallest share; the wheel needs two more than the root; the overflow needs twice the root. The whole flow is ten measures.'],
 ['The keeper’s counterweights','The three wheels do not open their own channels. Each handle advances its own channel by one and the next channel by two: Root then Wheel, Wheel then Overflow, Overflow then Root. Indicators cycle from zero through six and back to zero. The indicator lamps show the resulting measures, not the number of times each handle was turned. The old keeper used the same coupling to keep one careless hand from emptying a nursery.','Solve the allocation from the upstream diagram, then work out how to produce it with the coupled controls. Reset drains the indicators safely. No prize is lost for a mistake.'],
 ['The last sack','A sealed sack bears two receipts: a First Light requisition and a Dawn Bloom requisition. Each collector took payment for the same flour. Beside it lie orders assigning the mill’s next output either to the refugee kitchens or to families rebuilding the terrace nurseries. Neither group can eat a ledger. Hugh will honour either decision, but asks you to name who must wait.','The wheel must be restored and the milling challenge won before the allocation is signed. Reward: 3,000 doubloons and a lasting choice bonus.']
 ],
 peach:[
 ['The track that turned aside','A broad trail climbs towards a ruined watchpost, but the broken peach twigs lead downhill towards clean water. Liubeirow escaped the poisoned cistern by passing a traveller who did not bar its way. Its old oath was not to a throne: three companions promised to shelter the displaced, mend what armies poisoned and stand between the hunter and its prey. The first sanctuary opens to someone who has faced that hunter.','Read the three pools. A hand that heals comes after a hand that shelters. The one who draws the hunter away goes before both. Do not confuse a warrior’s weapon with the task it performs.'],
 ['Three pools, one oath','The western pool shows Feirong roaring from an empty ridge while families cross the valley below. The middle pool shows Guanrong holding a fallen gate above them. The eastern pool shows Liubeirow kneeling beside a poisoned spring after the last family has passed. The sequence follows what happened, not the positions of the pools.','Three bells wait in the next clearing. Each bears a title: HEALER, SHIELD, CALLER. Ring an oath that carries another life safely from danger to recovery. The stone judges only complete six-stroke oaths. A wrong oath may be cleared without closing the route behind you.'],
 ['The empty place','Three stone seats surround a low table. There is room for a fourth companion, but no crown. On the table, a peach stone has been split so that its seed can grow. A surviving inscription reads: Strength draws danger away; loyalty makes a shelter; mercy returns when the danger has passed. None is enough alone.','The oath has six strokes: carry the travellers out through the three deeds, then bring them home by the same deeds in reverse. No stroke is judged until the whole oath is sounded. Liubeirow may then be approached at the spring. This is a unique living creature. If it is defeated, it will not return. Leaving the encounter allows another attempt.'],
 ['The spring after the hunt','Liubeirow has been cleansing the headwater rather than hiding beneath a king’s wall. An orchard keeper has left no rope and no seal here, only bowls for the animals coming down from the dry ridge. It watches your partner, then steps away from the spring to face you. The water will remain clear whatever happens next.','Liubeirow is one of the Peach Orchard trio. Its companions remain beyond this chapter.']
 ],
 darius:[
 ['A camp without a banner','Maryam’s kitchens feed First Light deserters beside Dawn Bloom ditch crews. Darius has sent the younger children downriver. Alice says the evacuation was ordered before anyone was told why. Hugh has refused to put the grain carts on the causeway until the lower alarm can be heard from every shelter. None of them has left the Common Cause. None has agreed that the valley should become a hostage.','Maryam asks you to read the old spillway survey and restore a safe overflow before following Darius. He has already caught something. Do not open the reservoir’s upper gate while the downstream shelters are occupied.'],
 ['The spillway survey','The upper reservoir can hold five marks of rain before its face is overtopped. Three releases lead to the orchard, the abandoned quarry and the inhabited lower road. The orchard needs one mark; the quarry may safely take three; the lower road must receive none. The handles are coupled: Each handle advances its own release by one and the next release by two: Orchard then Quarry, Quarry then Road, Road then Orchard. Indicators run from zero through six. Keep one mark behind the upper face during a controlled release.','Restore the releases, then report to Alice at the lower warning station. Read the water levels carefully. The third gate is a road, not a spare ditch. The machine will not confirm which setting is wrong.'],
 ['A warning with names on it','Alice has a list of every household below the dam. Darius’s new map lists only the ranges of a landslide. She has copied the family names into its margin. Farid has guarded both sets of papers from patrols who would burn them for different reasons. The emergency overflow can carry a controlled release into the empty quarry, but only after the old wheel is reset.','Once the channels are safe, clear the patrol and send the evacuation signal. Hugh will move the last carts. The upper road then opens. Darius must hear what the warning would actually cost.'],
 ['A creature under command','Tellurion stands above the reservoir in a bronze control bridle. Roots have cracked the survey stakes around its feet. Darius has not ordered it to break the dam. He has ordered observers from both armies to watch it move one stone and imagine the rest. Maryam has brought dressings for the demonstration’s workers. She will not stay silent about why they need them.','Darius must be beaten before the bridle can be removed safely. His last partner is Tellurion. The challenge is dangerous; prepare before committing. Its later wild encounter is a separate chance to earn its trust, not a second specimen.'],
 ['The bridle after the warning','The bronze fastenings lie open. Tellurion has retreated to the garden shelf while Maryam tends its bruised neck. Darius refuses to give it to a king or a council. He agrees it must be allowed to choose whether to follow anyone. His remaining followers take the evacuation records away with them. Their argument has not ended.','This is the penultimate Common Cause confrontation. Darius leaves with his beliefs shaken and his people still divided; his final decision lies in a later chapter. Tellurion is unique: capture or death closes this encounter permanently.']
 ]
};
